# `exit(code)` — and the defect it closes.
#
# Until M-ffi-ladder a program that went wrong still told the shell it had
# succeeded: `main` may not declare a result (the checker refuses it, because a
# fallible `main` returning `fail(…)` printed nothing and exited 0), so there was
# no way for a Heroes program to report failure at all. The ROADMAP recorded it
# as a defect that "shows up on the second page of any tour".
#
# `exit` is written in Heroes over `hero_exit`, which is `_Noreturn` — without
# that, clang's flow analysis treats the code after the call as reachable, and C
# itself took 22 years and WG14 N1453 to admit as much.
#
# The harness asserts stdout; the exit status is asserted by the CLI surface
# test `exit_forwards_the_programs_own_status`, because a `run/` golden compares
# output rather than status.
# Bulk regression case.

function main()
    print("before")
    exit(3)
    print("after")
